{"title":"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At Euler Middle School, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee25c9b9adcc4a8f375271a0e11af30133a6fb2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$198$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> students voted on two issues in a school referendum with the following results: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac7aa4fe47f55808896713ce8fcd30b954e59a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$149$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> voted in favor of the first issue and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5dc392ba2faf31608de0cc131ab8c7227b31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$119$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> voted in favor of the second issue. If there were exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> students who voted against both issues, how many students voted in favor of both issues?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6632c2489836a4e7bc84e5ef04d42c775be73a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }49\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }70\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }79\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }99\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"407\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of students who voted in favor of the first issue,</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of students who voted in favor of the second issue,</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706277135716c6703c66dc5565e018a1580a51ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cap B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of students who voted in favor of both issues.</li></ul>\n<p>We are given:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d497ef5a39a56737770eb5de1a90864949bd2e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2300fbdcd9beec249edb57cf92c7fa27dfd4e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 119$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" /></li>\n<li>29 students voted against both issues, so the number of students who voted for at least one issue is:</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47147f0e40553197ff93a654922dddaa047fa41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[198 - 29 = 169\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>By the principle of inclusion and exclusion:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/1581622a2a93cc916feacd2bfe9c431bc2acdbdb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A \\cup B = A + B - A \\cap B\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"14\" />\nSubstitute known values:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/2532f606dfa0eb7edc3b0e50c2cc5a48a39b07d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[169 = 149 + 119 - A \\cap B\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c850b7fdf6afbd13297a82e18ae2480defe388.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[169 = 268 - A \\cap B\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee19f2876262312295433c29d4da25449bb2209c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A \\cap B = 268 - 169 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }99}\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that this is a Venn Diagram Problem.\n</p><p>First, we analyze the information given. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee25c9b9adcc4a8f375271a0e11af30133a6fb2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$198$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> students. Let's use A as the first issue and B as the second issue. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac7aa4fe47f55808896713ce8fcd30b954e59a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$149$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> students were for A, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5dc392ba2faf31608de0cc131ab8c7227b31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$119$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> students were for B. There were also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> students against both A and B. \n</p><p>Solving this without a Venn Diagram, we subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> away from the total, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee25c9b9adcc4a8f375271a0e11af30133a6fb2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$198$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Out of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> , we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac7aa4fe47f55808896713ce8fcd30b954e59a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$149$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> people for A and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f5dc392ba2faf31608de0cc131ab8c7227b31dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$119$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> people for B. We add this up to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb55bb967017b7f068d0aa458b9e943531d6fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$268$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> . Since that is more than what we need, we subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb55bb967017b7f068d0aa458b9e943531d6fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$268$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> to get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b36b731df41e5031b611678fc95925e0bb35c942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf5b45df5f86a8c2b3ba4e2f566d64e6ff019761.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); draw(Circle(origin, 5)); draw(Circle((5,0), 5)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,5), N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (5,5), N); label(&quot;$99$&quot;, (2.5, -0.5), N); label(&quot;$50$&quot;, (-2.5,-0.5), N); label(&quot;$20$&quot;, (7.5, -0.5), N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p>Note: One could use the Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion in a similar way to achieve the same result.\n</p><p>~ cxsmi (note)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1a8aef760655a43311d640070be0e72019cc8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$198-149=49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" /> students who voted against the first issue. Out of these, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/0837897eed525ee9f11c6c8394d2437c23b9d102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49-29=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> voted for the second issue. We also find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students voted against the second issue but in favor of the first in a similar way. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e197522cb187267b8661f9653e270a0a12b1270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$149-50=119-20=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"250\" height=\"30\" /> students voted in favor of both issues.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.youtube.com/watch?v=OOdK-nOzaII&amp;t=829s\">www.youtube.com/watch?v=OOdK-nOzaII&amp;t=829s</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/skOXiXCZVK0\">https://youtu.be/skOXiXCZVK0</a>\n</p><p>~ Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ATpixMaV-z4\">https://youtu.be/ATpixMaV-z4</a>\n</p><p>~ savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tb